From 6370eeb98d3f03b1b2d1c41116802a8bdcf50b52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 14:10:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06909/11362] [outer-loop] bp35: major correction, hard
 228-action timer found (round 8, fable-5)

claude-fable-5 round-8 session confirmed round 7's lead live (clicking
switch 2 from (6,31) after two lefts instead of four lands ALIVE at
(6,30), bypassing the notch), then made a much bigger discovery: the
historical "lethal right step out of the notch" was a MYTH. bp35 L6
has a hard, invisible action-count timer that ends the game at EXACTLY
total action 228 from reset, independent of position or action type --
reproduced 3x (mid-undo-rewind, mid-click-sweep, and decisively via a
pure no-op wait control with zero state change). Two prior rounds'
"lethal step" conclusion was actually the clock, not the step -- this
session stepped right out of the notch twice and stayed alive.

That leaves only 63 usable L6 actions after the 164-action prefix.
Mapped real new territory in that budget: pocket -> column-8 float ->
chimney float -> a row-21 corridor, reachable by ~action 189. The
corridor itself dead-ends against an exhaustive click-sweep, but
column 8 continuing upward from the corridor (untested) is flagged as
the round-9 move.

Independently re-verified by the outer loop: the saved 232-action
sequence is Run 1 (the first timer-death trace), and a fresh replay
correctly reproduces that exact death (level=0, GAME_OVER) -- matching
the session's own run_breakdown exactly, confirming this is an honest
diagnostic trace. The prefix alone still matches the known-good
level-5-verified sequence. No new level banked; frontier stays at
level 5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
